= Goodlake I Survives

A parliamentary coalition composed of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and all parties to its right—excluding the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>—somehow holds a majority. Mallin, emboldened by an electoral boost from an influx of more "reactionary" <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> voters, has once again grown overconfident, now believing he no longer needs the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> to enter government.

He assumes that [+ royalist_leader +], increasingly pressured by senior figures like Crowde and Frask, will eventually cave to preserve party unity and join the government on his terms. In the meantime, Mallin has taken the first step—accepting appointments as Vice-Chancellor and Finance Minister. Martin Schiele has been removed, replaced by the more conservative Kalckreuth.

- @goerdeler

@goerdeler
title: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] refuses to work with Mallin!
face-image: img/portraits/BrüningHeinrich.jpg

As expected, the majority of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] refuses to entertain the idea of governing alongside a figure like Mallin—especially after his remarks on <span class="tooltip-text" title="good game">the campaign trail</span> calling for the outright abolition of welfare. Furthermore, it is unlikely that Goodlake would stop this, as he himself has proposed gutting unemployment insurance to cut costs.

Even Askew, the de-facto leader of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]'s parliamentary delegation believes that their planned austerity has gone too far. 

Yet Mallin and Goodlake refuse to accept the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]'s demands for economic policy guarantees. Once again, a deadlock has taken hold.

- @goerdeler_2

@goerdeler_2
title: The Assembly is dissolved.
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_election_month = Q.month + 2;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 2;
if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
}
!}

Before the Assembly was to convene, Goodlake presents a decree to dissolve it. He expects that, with the exodus of voters from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> and the certainty of their collapse next election, they will be forced to become more sensible. 

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].